# Testing {{.Config.Project.Name}}

- Every Go package with non-exempt code ships meaningful tests of its behavior.
- Only files named `main.go` and files beneath any `cmd/` directory are exempt; keep behavior out of them.
- Cover success, invalid input, failure, and cancellation paths. No placeholder assertions or permanently skipped tests.
- Default tests must not need credentials, a live database, or a terminal.
